UObjectToolTips.CosmeticBackendItemHandle:
Smart handle to access and pin (future functionality) a FCosmeticBackendItem within a CosmeticInventoryCache. The handle provides readonly access to a Cosmetic Backend Item
which represents the backend data for a cosmetic item.
- Acts as a scoped Pin to keep item in cache if periodic purge runs to free space. (Cache purging is unimplemented so this functionality isn't used yet)
- Does not keep item in cache if item is explicitly removed, but will keep item alive so it's safe to reference even it removed from cache.
- Provides direct, read-only access to the underlying FCosmeticBackendItem data object.
Make sure to check the handle is valid before trying to access the FCosmeticBackendItem data, this handle acts like a shared pointer.

Ex.
FCosmeticBackendItemHandle ItemHandle = UCosmeticInventoryCache->RequestItem(...);
if (ItemHandle)
{
            ItemHandle->GetTemplateId();    // returns the template id of the underlying cosmetic backend item
}

